The issue: nginx is resolving `localhost` to IPv4 (127.0.0.1), but the Node app is listening only on IPv6 (:::3000). That's why nginx gets connection refused and returns 502. Fix: change the proxy_pass to use `http://[::1]:3000` or the explicit IPv6 address. Update the config file accordingly and reload nginx.

Updated location block:
```
location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://[::1]:3000;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
}
```

Run: `sudo systemctl reload nginx`.

